The unique SVN count for each chromosome equals the number of loci excluded from
EVN on that chromosome. Across the complete datasets, residual EVN/SVN overlap is
zero, and SVN contains no duplicate cCRE IDs. The chrY BED is retained as an empty
placeholder so the chromosome directory structure is predictable.

Each positive BED is stored as:

`chrom<chrom>/chrom<chrom>_GRCh38_Silencer_ELS.bed`

Positive FASTAs and 1x synthetic-negative BED/FASTA pools have been generated for chr1-chr22 and chrX. `genNullSeqs()` produced 196,024 synthetic negatives for 196,083 unique positives, a shortfall of 59 (0.030%). chrY has neither positive loci nor a negative pool. Real-genomic background counts will be added after the active antinoise jobs finish. The old overlapping source pools and their historical negative counts remain under `../overlaps/chroms/`.
